.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt OSSL_SELF_TEST_NEW 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm OSSL_SELF_TEST_new ,
.Nm OSSL_SELF_TEST_free ,
.Nm OSSL_SELF_TEST_onbegin ,
.Nm OSSL_SELF_TEST_oncorrupt_byte ,
.Nm OSSL_SELF_TEST_onend
.Nd functionality to trigger a callback during a self test
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/self_test.h
.Ft OSSL_SELF_TEST *
.Fo OSSL_SELF_TEST_new
.Fa "OSSL_CALLBACK *cb"
.Fa "void *cbarg"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo OSSL_SELF_TEST_free
.Fa "OSSL_SELF_TEST *st"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo OSSL_SELF_TEST_onbegin
.Fa "OSSL_SELF_TEST *st"
.Fa "const char *type"
.Fa "const char *desc"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo OSSL_SELF_TEST_oncorrupt_byte
.Fa "OSSL_SELF_TEST *st"
.Fa "unsigned char *bytes"
.Fc
.Ft void
.Fo OSSL_SELF_TEST_onend
.Fa "OSSL_SELF_TEST *st"
.Fa "int ret"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These methods are intended for use by provider implementers, to display
diagnostic information during self testing.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_SELF_TEST_new
allocates an opaque
.Vt OSSL_SELF_TEST
object that has a callback and callback argument associated with it.
.Pp
The callback
.Fa cb
may be triggered multiple times by a self test to indicate different
phases.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_SELF_TEST_free
frees the space allocated by
.Fn OSSL_SELF_TEST_new .
If the argument is NULL, nothing is done.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_SELF_TEST_onbegin
may be inserted at the start of a block of self test code.
It can be used for diagnostic purposes.
If this method is called the callback
.Fa cb
will receive the following
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3
object.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqst-phase" ( Ns Sy OSSL_PROV_PARAM_SELF_TEST_PHASE Ns ) <UTF8 string>
The value is the string "Start"
.El
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_SELF_TEST_oncorrupt_byte
may be inserted just after the known answer is calculated, but before
the self test compares the result.
The first byte in the passed in array of
.Fa bytes
will be corrupted if the callback returns 0, otherwise it leaves the
array unaltered.
It can be used for failure testing.
The
.Fa type
and
.Fa desc
can be used to identify an individual self test to target for failure
testing.
If this method is called the callback
.Fa cb
will receive the following
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3
object.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqst-phase" ( Ns Sy OSSL_PROV_PARAM_SELF_TEST_PHASE Ns ) <UTF8 string>
The value is the string "Corrupt"
.El
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_SELF_TEST_onend
may be inserted at the end of a block of self test code just before
cleanup to indicate if the test passed or failed.
It can be used for diagnostic purposes.
If this method is called the callback
.Fa cb
will receive the following
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3
object.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqst-phase" ( Ns Sy OSSL_PROV_PARAM_SELF_TEST_PHASE Ns ) <UTF8 string>
The value of the string is "Pass" if
.Fa ret
is non zero, otherwise it has the value "Fail".
.El
.Pp
After the callback
.Fa cb
has been called the values that were set by
.Fn OSSL_SELF_TEST_onbegin
for
.Fa type
and
.Fa desc
are set to the value "None".
.Pp
If
.Fn OSSL_SELF_TEST_onbegin ,
.Fn OSSL_SELF_TEST_oncorrupt_byte
or
.Fn OSSL_SELF_TEST_onend
is called the following additional
.Xr OSSL_PARAM 3
are passed to the callback.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It \(dqst-type" ( Ns Sy OSSL_PROV_PARAM_SELF_TEST_TYPE Ns ) <UTF8 string>
The value is setup by the
.Fa type
passed to
.Fn OSSL_SELF_TEST_onbegin .
This allows the callback to identify the type of test being run.
.It \(dqst-desc" ( Ns Sy OSSL_PROV_PARAM_SELF_TEST_DESC Ns ) <UTF8 string>
The value is setup by the
.Fa type
passed to
.Fn OSSL_SELF_TEST_onbegin .
This allows the callback to identify the sub category of the test being
run.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn OSSL_SELF_TEST_new
returns the allocated
.Vt OSSL_SELF_TEST
object, or NULL if it fails.
.Pp
.Fn OSSL_SELF_TEST_oncorrupt_byte
returns 1 if corruption occurs, otherwise it returns 0.
.Sh EXAMPLES
A single self test could be set up in the following way:
.Bd -literal
    OSSL_SELF_TEST *st = NULL;
    OSSL_CALLBACK *cb;
    void *cbarg;
    int ok = 0;
    unsigned char out[EVP_MAX_MD_SIZE];
    unsigned int out_len = 0;
    EVP_MD_CTX *ctx = EVP_MD_CTX_new();
    EVP_MD *md = EVP_MD_fetch(libctx, t->algorithm, NULL);

    /*
     * Retrieve the callback - will be NULL if not set by the application via
     * OSSL_SELF_TEST_set_callback().
     */
    OSSL_SELF_TEST_get_callback(libctx, &cb, &cbarg);

    st = OSSL_SELF_TEST_new(cb, cb_arg);

    /* Trigger the optional callback */
    OSSL_SELF_TEST_onbegin(st, OSSL_SELF_TEST_TYPE_KAT_DIGEST,
                           OSSL_SELF_TEST_DESC_MD_SHA2);

    if (!EVP_DigestInit_ex(ctx, md, NULL)
        || !EVP_DigestUpdate(ctx, pt, pt_len)
        || !EVP_DigestFinal(ctx, out, &out_len))
        goto err;

    /* Optional corruption - If the application callback returns 0 */
    OSSL_SELF_TEST_oncorrupt_byte(st, out);

    if (out_len != t->expected_len
        || memcmp(out, t->expected, out_len) != 0)
        goto err;
    ok = 1;
  err:
    OSSL_SELF_TEST_onend(st, ok);
    EVP_MD_free(md);
    EVP_MD_CTX_free(ctx);
.Ed
.Pp
Multiple self test's can be set up in a similar way by repeating the
pattern of
.Fn OSSL_SELF_TEST_onbegin ,
.Fn OSSL_SELF_TEST_oncorrupt_byte ,
.Fn OSSL_SELF_TEST_onend
for each test.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr OSSL_SELF_TEST_set_callback 3 ,
.Xr openssl-core.h 7 ,
.Xr OSSL_PROVIDER-FIPS 7
.Sh HISTORY
The functions described here were added in OpenSSL 3.0.
